course: dictionary
lesson: 14802
title: A punnet of strawberries
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A punnet is a small square basket or box, often made of plastic or cardboard, that holds soft fruit such as strawberries or raspberries. Look at the words around it: «I bought a punnet of strawberries at the market.» The strawberries go inside the punnet, so you know it is something that holds fruit.
explain: Context helps again. «Mum put a punnet of cherry tomatoes in the trolley.» Mum is shopping, and the tomatoes are sold in it, so a punnet is a box you buy food in. Ask yourself: what would fit in this gap? A box, a basket or a pack. Then check your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Words change from place to place. In the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, people say punnet. In the USA, people say «a basket» or «a carton» for the same thing. Same box, different name.
explain: Punnets also appear in maths. «A punnet holds 12 strawberries. How many strawberries are in 3 punnets?» Multiply: 12 × 3 = 36. Reading the context tells you which sum to do.
fact: A punnet is a small square basket or box for soft fruit.
fact: Punnets are often made of plastic or cardboard.
fact: The word «punnet» is used in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand.
fact: In the USA people say «basket» or «carton» instead of punnet.
fact: Phrases you may hear: «a punnet of strawberries» and «a punnet of cherry tomatoes».
exercise: «I bought a punnet of strawberries at the market.» What is a punnet? | A kind of cake with cream | A large farm where fruit grows | *A small square basket or box for soft fruit | A tall glass for juice
exercise: «A punnet holds 12 strawberries. How many strawberries are in 3 punnets?» | 15 | *36 | 9
exercise: In the USA people say «a carton» for what the UK calls a small square box of fruit. Which word is the UK word? | *Punnet | Jar | Tin | Bucket
test: «Mum put a punnet of cherry tomatoes in the trolley.» What is a punnet? | A big wooden table | A type of shoe | *A small square box or basket for food like fruit | A kind of bread roll
test: What does «a punnet of raspberries» mean? | A sheet of paper | A bag of flour | *Raspberries in a small square box | A jug of milk
exam: «Ben has 4 punnets of strawberries, and each punnet holds 12. How many strawberries does Ben have?» | 42 | 84 | *48 | 16
